   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The two paths that are services",
   "originalText": "The two paths that are services",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "nav",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 550,
   "width": 800,
   "height": 190,
   "strokeColor": "#1e293b",
   "backgroundColor": "#1e293b",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100031,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700217,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "nav_t",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "nav_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 577,
   "width": 784,
   "height": 135,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100032,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700224,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "client -> LB -> NAVIGATION service        compute-heavy, READ-ONLY\n  1. geocoding: '1355 Market St, SF' -> (37.7767, -122.4166)\n  2. derive the endpoint routing tiles from their geohashes\n  3. route planner: load coarse tiles along the corridor\n       -> A* across tiles, stitching neighbours as it traverses\n       -> refine near the endpoints with fine-grained tiles\n  4. ETA service: per-segment time from live + historical traffic\n  5. ranker: order candidates by the user's filters\n  6. encode the polyline; assemble turn-by-turn instructions",
   "originalText": "client -> LB -> NAVIGATION service        compute-heavy, READ-ONLY\n  1. geocoding: '1355 Market St, SF' -> (37.7767, -122.4166)\n  2. derive the endpoint routing tiles from their geohashes\n  3. route planner: load coarse tiles along the corridor\n       -> A* across tiles, stitching neighbours as it traverses\n       -> refine near the endpoints with fine-grained tiles\n  4. ETA service: per-segment time from live + historical traffic\n  5. ranker: order candidates by the user's filters\n  6. encode the polyline; assemble turn-by-turn instructions",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "nav",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 860,
   "y": 550,
   "width": 576,
   "height": 75,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100033,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700231,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Routing tiles come from OBJECT STORAGE, cached aggressively in the navigation\nservice's memory - deliberately not a database. There is no query to run: the\naccess pattern is 'give me tile 9q8yy at detail level 3', a key lookup for an\nopaque binary blob. A database would add query planning, transactions and\nindexing to serve GETs of immutable files.",
   "originalText": "Routing tiles come from OBJECT STORAGE, cached aggressively in the navigation\nservice's memory - deliberately not a database. There is no query to run: the\naccess pattern is 'give me tile 9q8yy at detail level 3', a key lookup for an\nopaque binary blob. A database would add query planning, transactions and\nindexing to serve GETs of immutable files.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 860,
   "y": 646,
   "width": 606,
   "height": 75,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100034,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700238,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "And navigation is ONE service, not five. The route planner, shortest-path search,\nETA lookup and ranking all operate on the same in-memory routing tiles inside one\nrequest's latency budget. Splitting them would mean shipping graph data between\nservices or re-loading tiles per hop - the same argument the stock exchange makes\nabout shared memory, at a much gentler latency scale.",
   "originalText": "And navigation is ONE service, not five. The route planner, shortest-path search,\nETA lookup and ranking all operate on the same in-memory routing tiles inside one\nrequest's latency budget. Splitting them would mean shipping graph data between\nservices or re-loading tiles per hop - the same argument the stock exchange makes\nabout shared memory, at a much gentler latency scale.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "ing",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 770,
   "width": 800,
   "height": 150,
   "strokeColor": "#1e293b",
   "backgroundColor": "#1e293b",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100035,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700245,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "ing_t",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ing_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 785,
   "width": 784,
   "height": 120,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100036,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700252,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "client batches ~15 GPS samples (75 s of movement)\n  -> POST /v1/locations -> LB -> LOCATION INGEST     write-only\n       -> 202 Accepted immediately     <- ack BEFORE any storage work\n       -> async: append to Cassandra (user_id + day bucket)\n       -> async: publish to Kafka\n            |- traffic aggregator -> per-segment speed -> edge weights\n            |- road-detection pipeline (new roads, closures, one-ways)\n            +- analytics warehouse",
   "originalText": "client batches ~15 GPS samples (75 s of movement)\n  -> POST /v1/locations -> LB -> LOCATION INGEST     write-only\n       -> 202 Accepted immediately     <- ack BEFORE any storage work\n       -> async: append to Cassandra (user_id + day bucket)\n       -> async: publish to Kafka\n            |- traffic aggregator -> per-segment speed -> edge weights\n            |- road-detection pipeline (new roads, closures, one-ways)\n            +- analytics warehouse",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "ing",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 860,
   "y": 770,
   "width": 606,
   "height": 75,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100037,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700259,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Acknowledging BEFORE storing is the right call here, and it is worth defending\nrather than treating as sloppiness. A GPS sample is worthless within a minute,\nself-corrected by the next batch, and its purpose is STATISTICAL - traffic speed\nis an aggregate over thousands of vehicles, so losing one vehicle's batch changes\nno number anyone sees.",
   "originalText": "Acknowledging BEFORE storing is the right call here, and it is worth defending\nrather than treating as sloppiness. A GPS sample is worthless within a minute,\nself-corrected by the next batch, and its purpose is STATISTICAL - traffic speed\nis an aggregate over thousands of vehicles, so losing one vehicle's batch changes\nno number anyone sees.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn4",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 860,
   "y": 866,
   "width": 562,
   "height": 30,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100038,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700266,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The ingest service also never READS. Coupling it to navigation would mean a\nCassandra write stall affecting route computation.",
   "originalText": "The ingest service also never READS. Coupling it to navigation would mean a\nCassandra write stall affecting route computation.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn5",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 860,
   "y": 916,
   "width": 599,
   "height": 45,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100039,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700273,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Geocoding is separate because it is a TEXT-SEARCH problem - fuzzy matching,\nabbreviations, many languages - over a small dataset with a completely different\nengine: an inverted index, not a graph.",
   "originalText": "Geocoding is separate because it is a TEXT-SEARCH problem - fuzzy matching,\nabbreviations, many languages - over a small dataset with a completely different\nengine: an inverted index, not a graph.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
