  },
  {
   "id": "fn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2132,
   "width": 1011,
   "height": 162,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100088,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700616,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "ETA service down            routes computed with static weights: directions CORRECT, times approximate. The ideal degradation\n                            shape - lose the enhancement, keep the function.\ntraffic aggregator down     weights go stale, so routes ignore new congestion. Degrades gradually rather than failing.\nlocation ingest down        traffic data stops improving. ZERO immediate user impact; the visible effect appears hours later.\ngeocoding down              address search fails, but navigation between coordinates still works - so 'navigate to a dropped\n                            pin' survives while 'navigate to an address' does not.\nnavigation service down     no NEW routes. In-progress navigation continues, because the client already holds its full route\n                            and instructions - deliberately not dependent on the server mid-journey.\nCDN down                    the origin is hammered and rendering degrades badly. THE WORST FAILURE, and the mitigation is\n                            multiple CDN providers with DNS failover.",
   "originalText": "ETA service down            routes computed with static weights: directions CORRECT, times approximate. The ideal degradation\n                            shape - lose the enhancement, keep the function.\ntraffic aggregator down     weights go stale, so routes ignore new congestion. Degrades gradually rather than failing.\nlocation ingest down        traffic data stops improving. ZERO immediate user impact; the visible effect appears hours later.\ngeocoding down              address search fails, but navigation between coordinates still works - so 'navigate to a dropped\n                            pin' survives while 'navigate to an address' does not.\nnavigation service down     no NEW routes. In-progress navigation continues, because the client already holds its full route\n                            and instructions - deliberately not dependent on the server mid-journey.\nCDN down                    the origin is hammered and rendering degrades badly. THE WORST FAILURE, and the mitigation is\n                            multiple CDN providers with DNS failover.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "fn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2332,
   "width": 1003,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100089,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700623,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Multi-region is genuinely easy here, because the data is geographic: tiles are global and edge-cached by nature, a region's\nrouting tiles are served from that region, and location history is homed regionally. THERE IS NO GLOBAL WRITE-CONSISTENCY\nREQUIREMENT ANYWHERE IN THE SYSTEM - a striking contrast with the digital wallet, where multi-region is the hardest unsolved\nproblem.",
   "originalText": "Multi-region is genuinely easy here, because the data is geographic: tiles are global and edge-cached by nature, a region's\nrouting tiles are served from that region, and location history is homed regionally. THERE IS NO GLOBAL WRITE-CONSISTENCY\nREQUIREMENT ANYWHERE IN THE SYSTEM - a striking contrast with the digital wallet, where multi-region is the hardest unsolved\nproblem.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
